Privacy Policy

Last Updated: September 24, 2026

ShieldAI VPN ("we", "our", or "the App") is committed to protecting your privacy. This Privacy Policy explains how information is handled when you use our Android application.

1. Information We Collect

We aim to collect only information necessary to operate and improve the App.

Information We May Process

Depending on the features you use, the App may process:

- VPN connection status
- Selected VPN/proxy server
- Connection duration
- Server latency and performance information
- Approximate country/region
- Public IP address while checking your connection
- App diagnostic and crash information
- Device and app information required for security and compatibility

We do not intentionally collect or store:

- Browsing history
- Websites you visit
- Website content
- Passwords
- Messages
- Photos or personal files
- DNS browsing history
- Contents of your internet traffic

2. VPN Traffic

When you connect to a VPN server, your internet traffic may pass through the selected VPN server.

The VPN infrastructure may technically process network information necessary to establish and maintain the connection, such as IP addresses and connection metadata.

We do not intentionally retain browsing activity or the contents of your internet traffic.

Important: No VPN service can guarantee complete anonymity or absolute security.

3. Public Proxy Servers

If the App provides access to third-party public proxy servers, those servers may be operated by independent parties.

We cannot guarantee the privacy, security, reliability, or practices of every third-party proxy server.

We recommend using trusted VPN servers for sensitive activities.

4. AI Features

The App may use Google Gemini or other AI services to provide features such as:

- Privacy recommendations
- Server recommendations
- Connection troubleshooting
- Privacy explanations
- AI Privacy Assistant

Only information necessary to provide the requested AI feature should be sent to the relevant AI service.

The App should not send passwords, private messages, browsing history, or the contents of VPN traffic to the AI system.

AI-generated recommendations may not always be accurate and should not be considered professional security advice.

5. Location Information

The App may use approximate location information to:

- Display relevant server locations
- Recommend nearby servers
- Improve server selection

We do not require precise GPS location for basic VPN functionality unless a feature explicitly requires it.

6. Analytics and Crash Reports

We may use services such as Firebase Analytics or Firebase Crashlytics to understand application performance and identify technical problems.

These services may process limited device, application, and diagnostic information.

You should configure these services according to your actual implementation and Google's applicable privacy requirements.

7. Advertising

The free version of the App may display advertisements through third-party advertising providers.

Advertising providers may process information such as advertising identifiers, device information, and general usage information in accordance with their own privacy policies.

We do not sell your browsing history or VPN traffic to advertisers.

8. Data Security

We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information processed by the App.

Where appropriate, we use:

- HTTPS/TLS
- Secure API communication
- Android Keystore
- Encrypted storage
- Access controls
- Secure authentication
- Regular security updates

However, no electronic system can be guaranteed to be completely secure.

9. Data Retention

We retain information only for as long as reasonably necessary for the purposes described in this Privacy Policy.

Connection history stored locally on your device can be deleted through the App where the feature is provided.

We do not intentionally retain your browsing history or the contents of your VPN traffic.

10. Third-Party Services

The App may use third-party services including:

- Google Firebase
- Google Gemini
- Google AdMob
- VPN/proxy infrastructure providers
- Cloud hosting providers

These providers may process information according to their respective privacy policies.

11. Children's Privacy

The App is not specifically directed toward children under the applicable minimum age for digital services in their jurisdiction.

We do not knowingly collect personal information from children for purposes unrelated to providing the service.

12. Your Choices

Depending on the features available in the App, you may be able to:

- Disconnect from the VPN at any time
- Delete locally stored connection history
- Disable optional analytics
- Disable notifications
- Control advertising preferences through Android or applicable advertising settings
- Delete your account, if an account system is provided

13. Changes to This Privacy Policy

We may update this Privacy Policy when the App's features, services, or legal requirements change.

The updated version will be made available through the App or our website, with the "Last Updated" date changed accordingly.

